From 1bbb0bb780f9d45b067ca8a19253f512583917b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:53:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hw: a button held at start is inverted only with
 invert_on_start

Why: the port's GPIO and PCF8574 readers took every button that read
pressed when its input started as wired the other way round (a 1-0-1,
normally closed button) and swapped its press and release for the
whole session. That is the owner's decision for his camera (like
Cinemate's check_initial_state), but on a stock camera a button held
or stuck at start then fires on release, and its next press does
nothing. In Apertar 1.6.0 the first sample seeds the debounce state,
so a button held at start fires nothing until it is released and
pressed again (GpioInput.cpp:693-697, Pcf8574Input.cpp:500-504 at
upstream-1.6.0); polarity comes from active_low only.

What: a section key invert_on_start, read with the section's
parseConfigBool, default false, in [gpio_buttons] (the buttons branch
only, not the keys [gpio_encoders] shares) and in [pcf8574], shaped
like upstream's [neorotary4] reset_on_start and [grove_analog]
emit_on_start. False: the first sample seeds observed and stable state
and a button held at start is not counted until it reads released, as
NeoRotary pushes already are; one journal line names it and says to
set invert_on_start=true for a normally closed button. True: the
inversion and journal line as before. Switches and NeoRotary pushes are
unchanged. The checker's key list knows the key; the default template
has it as a commented line under both sections; README says it.

Tested: check_core.sh both builds and the 18 host tests pass. A scratch
program drove GpioInput (poll mode) and Pcf8574Input through an
LD_PRELOAD fake of the chip and /dev/i2c-1: held at start, release,
press, release. Key absent: nothing, nothing, record_toggle, nothing.
invert_on_start=true: record_toggle on the first release and on the
last, the same as the parent commit. --simulate: set_controls
set.gpio_buttons.invert_on_start and set.pcf8574.invert_on_start are
written, set.gpio_encoders.invert_on_start is refused. Needs the
camera: [gpio_buttons] enabled=true d17=record_toggle, hold d17,
sudo systemctl restart apertar-core, release: nothing records; press:
it records. With invert_on_start=true and a normally closed button:
journalctl -u apertar-core | grep 'taken as inverted' names it and one
press records once. Same on a PCF8574 pin. On the owner's rig, any
'taken as inverted' line in the journal today means he adds
invert_on_start=true.

